  ('6c58fe75-fec1-5a8c-98c2-cacfa45a8c98', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-word-parts'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The suffix -tion turns an action into a thing. The verb observe means "to watch closely." What is each "observation" that scientists write?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A rule that tells scientists how to look","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-base-word"},{"text":"The act of keeping a pond clean and safe","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-conservation"},{"text":"A guess about what a creature might do next","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-prediction"},{"text":"A note about something they watched closely","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A note about something they watched closely$q$, $q$Observe plus -tion names the thing you get from watching closely, and the passage says each one records a creature's size, shape and movement. A guess about the future would be a prediction, not an observation.$q$, 'draft', '424a7571-d6d7-562f-ad2e-e8ae4ed77705')
