-- Passage rg5-word-parts-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('3438700d-14ca-5161-9d81-0dc771d0b28d', 'rg5-word-parts-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-word-parts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Craft Stick Bridge$q$, $q$Mr. Hasegawa held up a box of craft sticks and a bottle of glue. "Your challenge," he said, "is to construct a bridge that can hold the most weight."

Jonah and Lucia worked as partners. First they sketched a plan. Lucia wanted a simple flat bridge, but Jonah pointed to a picture of a real bridge with triangles along its sides. "Triangles make a structure stronger," he said. They decided to try it.

Building took three days. The glue had to dry overnight between each step. On the second day, one side of the bridge was crooked, so they pulled it apart and rebuilt it.

Testing day arrived. Each team hung a bucket from its bridge, and Mr. Hasegawa added sand one cup at a time. Some bridges sagged quickly. One bridge suddenly cracked with a loud snap. The rupture began at a single weak joint and spread across the whole bridge.

Jonah and Lucia's bridge held twelve cups. When it finally broke, the destruction was so complete that only a pile of sticks remained. Still, they had won the challenge.$q$, 'draft')
