   $q$The Latin root struct means "build," and the prefix con- means "together." What were the students asked to do when they had to "construct" a bridge?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Draw a picture of it on paper","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-graph-root"},{"text":"Break it apart to see inside","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Measure how long it should be","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-meter-root"},{"text":"Build it by putting parts together","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Build it by putting parts together$q$, $q$Construct means "build together," and the students glued sticks into bridges. Breaking a bridge apart is the opposite, and it is what happened only at the end.$q$, 'draft', '3438700d-14ca-5161-9d81-0dc771d0b28d')
