   $q$The Greek root geo means "earth." Which clue in the passage confirms the meaning of "geologist"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Families who pack supplies and wait for the buses","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"A scientist who studies the earth and its rocks","is_correct":true},{"text":"Hot melted rock that slowly moves and pushes upward","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Tools on the sides of a mountain that measure shakes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-tool-with-person"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A scientist who studies the earth and its rocks$q$, $q$The passage defines a geologist as "a scientist who studies the earth and its rocks," which matches geo, "earth." The tools are what geologists use, not who they are.$q$, 'draft', '17773410-8578-588b-a135-7ef47bcf2369')
