   $q$The Latin prefix e- means "out," and rupt means "break." Which phrase from the passage best matches the meaning of "eruption"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"rise from cracks in the rock\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-gases-with-eruption"},{"text":"\"tiny shakes in the ground\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sign-with-event"},{"text":"\"burst out of the mountain\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"slowly moves and pushes upward\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"burst out of the mountain"$q$, $q$An eruption is a breaking out, and the passage says it is when rock, ash and gas "burst out of the mountain." Slow upward movement happens before an eruption; it is a warning sign, not the break itself.$q$, 'draft', '17773410-8578-588b-a135-7ef47bcf2369')
