   $q$The Latin prefix dis- means "apart," and rupt means "break." What does it mean that an eruption can "disrupt" daily life?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It can break up normal routines and stop them","is_correct":true},{"text":"It can break the mountain into two halves","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It can help towns plan their daily schedule","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"It can make daily life calmer and quieter","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It can break up normal routines and stop them$q$, $q$Disrupt means to break apart something orderly, and the passage lists closed schools, covered roads and stopped airplanes. It is daily life that breaks up, not the mountain itself.$q$, 'draft', '17773410-8578-588b-a135-7ef47bcf2369')
